Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 15:12:51 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(tui): review fixes for the build-time quota wall card
 [daveey]

Independent review of #3846 (REQUEST_CHANGES), all findings addressed:
- quota_refusal_wall names only one route's own refusal: a ProviderFallbackError gives None (real chains
  list the pin then configured fallbacks; a mixed chain's cause may not be a quota), so no fallback is
  called "pinned" and a primary's credential error keeps its generic message. Provider/model as the
  refusal gives them, matching held_reply.
- A build start drops an earlier build's failure_route, so a later abandoned/timed-out build or a later
  route_refused frame never reuses a stale wall; the route is recorded after agent_error, guarded.
- turn_error_text: a route_refused descriptor carrying `message` reads as that sentence alone (no repeated
  /model hint), like the gateway path's final_response.
- The surface is built with agent.error_surface._surface (provider, model, provider_label) + message.

Tests (RED on the pre-review source, GREEN after): fallback chains (mixed, all walled), stale route cleared
on a new build, own-sentence turn text, malformed route record keeps the generic card.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
